## Critical Issues

### 1. Missing boundary/integration test for the Sentry registry seam
The core of this fix is a new value (`event.Fingerprint`) that crosses into Sentry's event-processor registry and grouping. `TestSentryFingerprintProcessor` only calls the processor function directly — it proves the transformation, not that `sentry.AddGlobalEventProcessor(sentryFingerprintProcessor)` is reachable through the real `CaptureException` path, nor that `EventHint.OriginalException` carries the `*statusError` at capture time. If either link is wrong, fingerprinting silently never happens and `NUKE-PROD-CV` persists — exactly the silent failure class this audit targets. Per the boundary-crossing rule (registry/dispatch), a level-2 integration test is required.

